it for actual visible-media/decode barriers; a selected suite that omits stale tests cannot certify all consumer integration. Stop at horizontal endpoints and reverse; lock required input, cancel in-flight smooth scroll and retain focus/Close/Retry. Exercise real corrupt HTTP200 cache without routing, explicit Retry despite automatic browser attempts, native replacement-load/decode order, no-JS and HTTP200 script throw/rejection before hydration. Inspect effective loading contrast including reduced-motion opacity; old scroll/wheel/CTA tests must wait for actual readiness before ordinary input, while separate pending tests verify locks. Serialize framework build before generated-type checks. Verify each changed journal ID contains its own dated technical approval and matching index lifecycle; bound insertion at the earliest next ID anchor or heading, never leave prior-ID verdicts below the next ID anchor. A neighboring entry or index alone is insufficient. For the vertical-white-band follow-up, independently measure all four photo/cutout edges and zero internal scroll when the proportional full-width source fits. Bound frame height to the photo plus source-scaled metal borders; never stretch or crop to remove surplus white space. Inspect393×852, Pro/Max and short-window top/bottom captures. Post-hydration viewer tests await hydration and media readiness; preserve parallel timeout failures and rerun without concurrent browser load before approval. For CHG0073 instruction validation, use the existing artwork-color-pipeline geometry mode even for CSS-only photo adaptation; keep separate photo/frame width, proportional height and content access checks, without re-encoding unchanged originals. Consolidate diagnosis and verification into the existing viewer topic, retain raw evidence and historical verdicts, and repair relocated links. For the retained-main follow-up, inject a delayed far landing tile and held/corrupt optional gallery prefetch. Reject covering ready conten