LESSONS.md:11:## Keep the critical verification sequence visible at each decision point
LESSONS.md:13:- **Problem:** A context review treated repetition of the visual verification sequence as disposable duplication.
LESSONS.md:21:- **Prevention:** Keep short, verified, up-to-date handoff facts in [MEMORY.md](MEMORY.md); keep recurring problem → cause → prevention entries here; record every logical change/defect, its solution, verification and approval in [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md). Make [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) trigger both retrieval and maintenance, and correct stale memory against current files and user instructions.
LESSONS.md:33:- **Prevention:** Resolve framework and toolchain choices first. Install or retain only skills that serve the chosen stack or a required verification gap; remove obsolete skills and their active-document references when a decision changes. Preserve the original brief as a source record.
LESSONS.md:217:- **Problem:** CHG-0047 replaced lossy WebP tiles after the designer reported a color/quality mismatch; the first PNG verification also briefly accepted blank WebKit frames because `complete` and `naturalWidth` were true before paint. CHG-0058 found that `doc-emc.webp` passed a whole-image mean check despite red/blue p99 errors of 29/255 on visible pixels.
LESSONS.md:243:- **Prevention:** When replacing a dialog, CTA destination, or asset URL, search all tests and runtime consumers for its old ID/path and assertions before editing, then run affected checks before the full suite. CHG-0061 repeated this failure in the 2026-10-07 PNG→WebP correction: updating only the direct viewer spec missed site.spec.ts. Check initial-page requests for optional modal images before accepting a priority flag; mount them only while open. [EVAL-VIEWER](docs/agent-evals.md#eval-viewer) controlled agent run `NOT_RUN`.
LESSONS.md:249:- **Prevention:** Keep visible title, image, pagination and group action tied to the same decoded selection. CHG-0068 double-next used an unseen requested group and falsely announced no next group; ignore repeated pending group moves, cancel on reversal, and test visible horizontal controls during pending vertical navigation. Restore focus after a group commit removes the focused dot or previous button; verify the new dialog title is committed before refocusing and continue keyboard arrows. Do not swap a React-owned image src for QA controls; use source-response interception in an equivalent reference page. Keep the previous decoded frame until the next resource decodes, provide a small first-frame preview, and test the intermediate state with an intentionally delayed image request. Await `complete && naturalWidth` before visual capture. CHG-0067 public QA also applied a local5s switch deadline before asynchronous original PNGs finished downloading. For cached-switch release checks, first observe the actual image responses/body completion with a bounded network deadline and then await decoded media; keep delayed/failed cold-switch behavior as its own tested state. A readiness timeout is not a visual pass or proof of a runtime defect. [EVAL-VIEWER](docs/agent-evals.md#eval-viewer) remains `NOT_RUN`.
LESSONS.md:255:- **Prevention:** For a supplied reusable frame, make the immutable frame from the source pixels with a transparent content opening, insert variable content underneath, and compare the masked immutable region against the original at the calibrated viewport. When reversing a stage that uses object-fit:fill/SVG preserveAspectRatio:none into source coordinates, explicitly resize both axes with fit:fill; CHG-0068 default cover cropped the QA pair and created a false title Y shift. Separate reusable artwork from live content before extraction: contour pixels stay artwork; instructions and labels use semantic translatable HTML in the mapped page font; arrows/dots are separate source-derived sprites. Do not bake copy into a frame merely because a composite reference includes it. Match visible spacing as well as sprite color; use compact nonoverlapping pagination targets when reference spacing conflicts with an earlier arbitrary target width. Reopen prior approval when customer rejects visible fidelity. [EVAL-VIEWER](docs/agent-evals.md#eval-viewer) is `NOT_RUN`.
LESSONS.md:261:- **Prevention:** Map each visible instruction, arrow and pagination mark to an action or an explicit unavailable state before approving UI. The number and active state of indicators must derive from actual data; test tap and keyboard activation, loading and failure transitions, and placeholder honesty. At narrow/short screens, compare whole touch-target rectangles for unintended overlap, not only their center-click outcomes. Preserve source artwork outside only the clearly authorized dynamic regions. [EVAL-VIEWER](docs/agent-evals.md#eval-viewer) controlled agent run remains `NOT_RUN`.
LESSONS.md:267:- **Prevention:** Before a commit or push, use `git ls-files` or staged-tree inspection for the small set of screenshots needed to support visual claims. Copy exact final captures into a tracked evidence path and link them from the report; keep bulky exploratory captures ignored. [EVAL-VIEWER](docs/agent-evals.md#eval-viewer) remains `NOT_RUN`.
LESSONS.md:273:- **Prevention:** When original-only or no-conversion delivery is required, copy the supplied files byte-for-byte, keep dimensions/profiles intact, disable framework transformations, and verify source/public/HTTP hashes and actual decoded browser images. Remove conflicting derivatives and small previews from that feature. Measure original payload honestly; defer encoding optimization until authorized. [EVAL-VIEWER](docs/agent-evals.md#eval-viewer) controlled agent run NOT_RUN.
LESSONS.md:279:- **Prevention:** Repair each distinct background separately, preserve untouched master pixels, and inspect restored glyph regions at native size for texture/groove continuity. For narrow repeating grooves, anchor their phase to untouched source columns above/below the glyph; bounded fine texture can fill only the occluded region. Exact identity outside a mask is necessary but does not certify the reconstructed region. [EVAL-VIEWER](docs/agent-evals.md#eval-viewer) controlled agent run NOT_RUN.
LESSONS.md:285:- **Prevention:** Inspect actual rendered ancestry before ancestor selectors; while fullscreen viewer opens, verify underlying document backing separately from modal paint, including descendants with explicit visibility. Preserve layout, close colors/scroll/focus, and inspect changing portrait heights plus short landscape control/frame rectangles. Emulation cannot certify native Safari/Telegram chrome; record hardware checks as unavailable until actual evidence exists. EVAL-VIEWER controlled run remains NOT_RUN.
LESSONS.md:290:- **Problem → cause → prevention:** A locale test asserted text immediately after triggering asynchronous group navigation while the previous decoded image still displayed. Wait for the viewer's displayed group/image state before inspecting dependent text. Preserve the failed run and repeat the affected check; controlled EVAL-VIEWER run remains `NOT_RUN`.
LESSONS.md:294:- **Problem → cause → prevention:** At the same iPhone width, expanded Safari/Telegram chrome shortened `100dvh`; the agent's gallery used viewport width and dynamic viewport height independently, then `object-fit:fill` stretched the photograph, frame, and SVG text. Prior 13 Pro verification asserted edge placement, image bytes and controls but omitted rendered aspect ratio at alternate browser chrome heights. For any fullscreen composition with reference artwork, test at least two visual viewport heights at one width, assert rendered artwork/frame aspect ratios against source dimensions, and inspect real screenshots. Use one uniform scale factor or explicitly document intentional crop; never infer fidelity from PNG hashes or edge alignment. [EVAL-VIEWER](docs/agent-evals.md#eval-viewer) controlled agent run remains `NOT_RUN`.
LESSONS.md:297:- **White-band follow-up / CHG-0070:** Width and aspect checks missed surplus top/bottom white space in a taller cutout. Measure all four photo/cutout edges independently. When a full-width proportional photo fits, cap frame height at photo height plus unchanged border thickness and center the frame in the control gap; assert zero nominal inner scroll. Capture393×852, Pro and Max plus shorter same-width windows. Post-hydration interaction tests must await a hydration marker as well as media readiness; exact old missed-click cause was not traced. Controlled EVAL-VIEWER remains NOT_RUN.
LESSONS.md:301:- **Problem → cause → prevention:** Initial gallery open inserted a live image and overlay copy before the preload completed; only later transitions had a decode barrier. A separate preloaded element did not guard the newly painted element. For initial and subsequent frames, reveal the actual retained decoded image and its overlay text together. Verify a cold response held at partial bytes and a failed decode, with real pending/ready screenshots and true progress or an explicit indeterminate fallback. A fetched URL or source hash alone is not readiness. [EVAL-VIEWER](docs/agent-evals.md#eval-viewer) controlled run NOT_RUN.
LESSONS.md:305:- **Follow-up / CHG-0070/0066:** A stretched metal image still distorts corners; preserve corners through nine-slice borders when the outer rectangle must adapt. Inspect arrow/dot sprites too, and assert the entire pagination hit rectangle between header and frame. Only checking the instruction missed tablet/desktop overlap. Controlled EVAL-VIEWER NOT_RUN.
LESSONS.md:306:- **Follow-up / CHG-0071:** Evicting an application Map does not evict a corrupt HTTP200 from browser cache. Test real cacheable responses without Playwright routing, bypass failed URLs only, retain successful decoded elements. Firefox decode immediately after src mutation may refer to the previous currentSrc; wait for replacement load/error first. Preserve static no-JS artwork when adding pre-hydration guards. Controlled EVAL-VIEWER NOT_RUN.
LESSONS.md:307:- **Follow-up / CHG-0071:** Check effective painted contrast, including opacity and reduced-motion variants. Reading only a computed background color missed a half-opacity loading bar; keep a static indeterminate segment at full opacity and assert both its contrast and opacity. Browser tests validate the UI; controlled EVAL-VIEWER remains NOT_RUN.
LESSONS.md:308:- **Follow-up / CHG-0071:** A bootstrap hiding SSR content needs an initial execution-failure fallback as well as a script-download fallback. Test successful HTTP200 scripts that throw or reject before hydration; keep native content/FAQ readable. Distinguish framework/global execution errors from normal image-resource errors so a failed image cannot bypass a functioning gate. Controlled EVAL-VIEWER NOT_RUN.
LESSONS.md:309:- **Follow-up / CHG-0071:** Adding a visible-media input gate changes assumptions in all old scroll-dependent browser checks, including FAQ wheel and offscreen CTA tests. Wait for visibility observers and the actual gate before testing user input; preserve the explicit pending-lock checks separately. Error fixtures must remain failed until explicit Retry even if the browser automatically retries. Framework builds rewrite generated route types: serialize build before TypeScript verification. Controlled EVAL-VIEWER NOT_RUN.
LESSONS.md:311:- **Record closure / CHG-0071:** Journal sections may use both plain headings and explicit anchors. Bound scripted updates by the earliest next logical ID anchor or heading, then verify index lifecycle and each changed ID contains its own dated approval; an index status or approval in a neighboring section is insufficient. CHG0076 final audit caught recurrence when the agent used only the heading boundary and omitted the index; require a direct anchor-to-anchor ownership check after insertion. This changes the procedure, not model weights; controlled EVAL-VIEWER NOT_RUN.
LESSONS.md:315:- **Problem → cause → prevention:** The agent widened the contour but contained the941×1672 photo by height, leaving white side bands the user rejects. Aspect/source-byte checks and full-width contour tests cannot certify full-width photo. Map and measure each separately. At unequal source/window ratios, explicitly reconcile full width, no distortion, all content visible at once and no scrolling: fixed composition cannot guarantee all four. Prefer width-fit plus inner vertical scroll when content must remain accessible; use per-slide safe-region responsive recomposition if all-at-once is required. Never blindly cover/crop source-aligned labels/diagrams. Verify new gesture policy, pending inner-scroll locks, all six slides/locales and changing chrome heights. [EVAL-VIEWER](docs/agent-evals.md#eval-viewer) prevention extended; controlled agent run NOT_RUN.
LESSONS.md:317:- **Follow-up / CHG-0070 width implementation:** Retrieve every consumer when changing contour element type, retained-image URL or gesture policy. The mapped-dialog integration test retained IMG/src assertions and offscreen focus/rapid-key assumptions after the nine-slice/loading revision. Check CSS border-image/source data attributes as appropriate, scroll to the trigger and wait for actual visible media before ordinary keyboard activation, then wait for each decoded commit. Preserve failed runs and repeat integration; new pending tests separately verify blocked input. Current rechecks validate product behavior; controlled EVAL-VIEWER remains NOT_RUN.
LESSONS.md:319:- **Record follow-up / CHG-0070:** After superseding a geometry policy, reread the complete affected current specification, including narrative below updated headers/tables. An exact text replacement or updated summary does not prove every old policy paragraph was reconciled. Independent record consistency remains a separate acceptance check. Controlled EVAL-VIEWER NOT_RUN.
LESSONS.md:323:- **Problem → cause → prevention:** The agent split one viewer correction across a new width-analysis document and evidence checks document despite an existing maintained viewer topic. Keep diagnosis, chosen geometry and verification in that topic, raw screenshots/logs in its existing evidence directory, and change history in CHANGELOG. Create another document only for a distinct maintained topic or explicit request. When moving a record, update live link targets and preserve historical filenames as plain code; broad path replacement can erase the documented mistake. Photo geometry now routes through artwork-color-pipeline even for CSS-only work; check photo width/aspect/content separately and preserve its raster color workflow. Skill edits do not establish improved behavior; [EVAL-VIEWER](docs/agent-evals.md#eval-viewer) controlled run NOT_RUN.
LESSONS.md:331:- **Problem → cause → prevention:** The agent applied an opaque, bidirectional initial guard to later main-page images. Its tests approved hidden content and blocked input instead of the requested retained view. Keep the initial guard separate from subsequent readiness: cap native document height before unfinished artwork, keep completed pixels and controls available, show a bottom loading strip only at the reached frontier, and allow upward native scrolling. Prefetch all main artwork after actual hero DOM decode with high priority; warm all six gallery photos separately at low priority without affecting the main gate. Test held/corrupt optional gallery resources, native wheel/touch reversal, programmatic jumps, clipped focus targets, FAQ/resize frontier changes and unchanged ready pixels before/after decode. Await actual DOM readiness before measuring full-page height; load is not decode readiness. Extract comparison regions from full viewport screenshots in the same coordinate system. Serialize speed measurements away from browser suites, preserve failed attempts and historical screenshot files. Follow the auditor profile’s one-named-gate checkpoint with bounded artifacts; earlier resumed multi-gate turns produced no finding (delay cause unknown), while fresh sequential checkpoints supplied actual verdicts. Product regression passes do not execute the controlled [EVAL-VIEWER](docs/agent-evals.md#eval-viewer); its status remains NOT_RUN.
LESSONS.md:338:- **Problem → cause → prevention:** A new Firefox fixture rejected0.5CSSpx despite the defined<1px contract and expected one giant wheel event to reach the bottom. Assert the documented tolerance, repeat bounded real wheel events until an observed endpoint, and never replace wheel verification with programmatic scrolling. Inspect actual pixels before dismissing differences as rounding.
LESSONS.md:340:- Linked [EVAL-VIEWER](docs/agent-evals.md#eval-viewer) extended with these acceptance checks. Product checks pass for ribbons; controlled agent run remains NOT_RUN and no model-weight change is claimed.
LESSONS.md:342:- **Dispatch follow-up /CHG0076:** An unstaged diff check excludes new untracked screenshots/logs. Before committing evidence, inspect the exact staged scope and run git diff --cached --check; normalize only log formatting while retaining raw originals and all verdicts. Runtime hashes and unrelated exclusions remain separate assertions. Controlled EVAL-VIEWER NOT_RUN.
LESSONS.md:344:- **Scope-record follow-up /CHG0077:** Starting a parallel scope audit before creating its journal ID led to an absent-record FAIL, even though implementation had not started. Seed actual/expected/source/lifecycle at discovery before dispatching the scope audit; refine measured geometry afterward. Controlled EVAL-VIEWER NOT_RUN.
LESSONS.md:348:- **Problem → cause → prevention:** Laptop viewer expanded to100vw while the main canvas stopped at941px. Agent inherited viewport-wide acceptance and missed comparing real landing bounds. Mobile-first galleries use the current main canvas cap unless a user explicitly requests another width. Share the cap, compare dialog/photo left/right/width to actual landing below and above its breakpoint, and inspect mobile pixel preservation plus desktop native wheel/bottom. Full-window matte does not authorize enlarging photo planes. EVAL-VIEWER extended; controlled run NOT_RUN.
