- **Problem → cause → prevention:** The agent applied an opaque, bidirectional initial guard to later main-page images. Its tests approved hidden content and blocked input instead of the requested retained view. Keep the initial guard separate from subsequent readiness: cap native document height before unfinished artwork, keep completed pixels and controls available, show a bottom loading strip only at the reached frontier, and allow upward native scrolling. Prefetch all main artwork after actual hero DOM decode with high priority; warm all six gallery photos separately at low priority without affecting the main gate. Test held/corrupt optional gallery resources, native wheel/touch reversal, programmatic jumps, clipped focus targets, FAQ/resize frontier changes and unchanged ready pixels before/after decode. Await actual DOM readiness before measuring full-page height; load is not decode readiness. Extract comparison regions from full viewport screenshots in the same coordinate system. Serialize speed measurements away from browser suites, preserve failed attempts and historical screenshot files. Follow the auditor profile’s one-named-gate checkpoint with bounded artifacts; earlier resumed multi-gate turns produced no finding (delay cause unknown), while fresh sequential checkpoints supplied actual verdicts. Product regression passes do not execute the controlled [EVAL-VIEWER](docs/agent-evals.md#eval-viewer); its status remains NOT_RUN.


## Ribbon navigation and actual paint — CHG-0076 / CHG-0071

- **Problem → cause → prevention:** Removing a numeric callout span also shifted the following label. The agent edited layout before asserting its independent source-local x/width. Remove the index while retaining the label's original x94/195sourcepx box; compare all six body planes with only intentional regions masked. Full-width geometry alone cannot establish unchanged text placement.
- **Problem → cause → prevention:** Native dialog containment passed short focus checks but a complete new-control Tab cycle escaped in ProMax/Chromium. Exercise every enabled control plus scroll region through full Tab and ShiftTab cycles, while ready and pending; wrap first/last explicitly and test after group change/Close restoration. A partial cycle cannot approve containment.
- **Problem → cause → prevention:** A new Firefox fixture rejected0.5CSSpx despite the defined<1px contract and expected one giant wheel event to reach the bottom. Assert the documented tolerance, repeat bounded real wheel events until an observed endpoint, and never replace wheel verification with programmatic scrolling. Inspect actual pixels before dismissing differences as rounding.
- **Problem → cause → prevention:** A decoded DOM marker was treated as sufficient paint readiness; immediate WebKit assembly captures sometimes lacked artwork, and existing held-resource captures failed on both current and untouched baseline versions. Await actual fonts/images and paint settlement for stable compositions, preserve failures and separately audit transient/pending paint. Do not claim a test timing barrier fixes the runtime; exact held-resource cause remains UNKNOWN and CHG0071 reopened. Compare unchanged host baseline before attributing an unrelated defect to a new feature. Preserve historical approved screenshots before suites overwrite them; keep current failures under new evidence paths and restore historical bytes.
- Linked [EVAL-VIEWER](docs/agent-evals.md#eval-viewer) extended with these acceptance checks. Product checks pass for ribbons; controlled agent run remains NOT_RUN and no model-weight change is claimed.

- **Dispatch follow-up /CHG0076:** An unstaged diff check excludes new untracked screenshots/logs. Before committing evidence, inspect the exact staged scope and run git diff --cached --check; normalize only log formatting while retaining raw originals and all verdicts. Runtime hashes and unrelated exclusions remain separate assertions. Controlled EVAL-VIEWER NOT_RUN.

- **Scope-record follow-up /CHG0077:** Starting a parallel scope audit before creating its journal ID led to an absent-record FAIL, even though implementation had not started. Seed actual/expected/source/lifecycle at discovery before dispatching the scope audit; refine measured geometry afterward. Controlled EVAL-VIEWER NOT_RUN.

## Technical gallery inherits the landing canvas width — CHG-0078

- **Problem → cause → prevention:** Laptop viewer expanded to100vw while the main canvas stopped at941px. Agent inherited viewport-wide acceptance and missed comparing real landing bounds. Mobile-first galleries use the current main canvas cap unless a user explicitly requests another width. Share the cap, compare dialog/photo left/right/width to actual landing below and above its breakpoint, and inspect mobile pixel preservation plus desktop native wheel/bottom. Full-window matte does not authorize enlarging photo planes. EVAL-VIEWER extended; controlled run NOT_RUN.
- **Evidence retention follow-up:** Root launched another runner before copying its failed wheel screenshot; shared test-results was cleared. Archive failure artifacts before the next runner, use separate output directories for independent runs, and retain failure logs even if a screenshot is lost. The failed screenshot here is unavailable, not certified retained.

- **Documentation edit verification / CHG0078 Stage6:** An exact-string replacement used a mismatched needle and silently left EVAL prevention absent. Assert the expected occurrence before replacement and verify the resulting targeted diff/postcondition before claiming a documentation update. The record fix does not prove future agent compliance; controlled EVAL-VIEWER remains NOT_RUN.

